; onehotc_spin_model: ONEHOTC on a spin {-1, +1} model raises NonBinaryModel.
;
; ONEHOTC writes a one-hot penalty over grid column 0, and spec/xqvm/HLF.md derives
; every constraint expansion under x^2 = x, which fails for spin variables
; and for integer variables with k > 2. The check follows the declared domain
; (only a model whose domain is binary passes), so spec/xqvm/ISA.md has ONEHOTC raise NonBinaryModel instead. Every other
; operand is valid, so the domain check alone decides.

PUSH 4
SQMX r0          ; spin model, 4 variables
PUSH 2           ; rows
PUSH 2           ; cols
RESIZE r0        ; 2x2 grid, so the grid precondition holds
PUSH 0           ; col
PUSH 1           ; penalty
ONEHOTC r0
HALT
